{"t": 1785378717.2, "lenguaje": "html", "temperature": 0.2, "reasoning_effort": null, "max_tokens": null, "system": "You are a creative front-end developer. Write complete, self-contained HTML pages with inline CSS and JavaScript and no external resources. The page must animate by itself on load. Follow the output format exactly.", "prompt": "You are a creative front-end developer making self-contained web pages.\n\nWrite a complete HTML page for: **Un buscaminas 5x5 con 3 minas en posiciones FIJAS en un solo archivo HTML. OBLIGATORIO: 25 celdas <div class=\"c\"> con data-i de 0 a 24; las minas estan en las celdas 6, 12 y 18. Al hacer click en una celda se revela: gana la clase 'abierta' y muestra el numero de minas adyacentes (contando las 8 vecinas), o nada si es 0. REGLA CLAVE: si se abre una celda con 0 minas adyacentes, se abren tambien EN CASCADA todas sus vecinas con 0, y los bordes de esa region. Click derecho pone una bandera (clase 'bandera') y una celda con bandera NO se abre al hacer click. <div id=\"estado\"> dice 'perdiste' si se abre una mina.. TARGET LOOK, match it: A compact 5x5 grid of square cells arranged in a single column‑major block, centered on a light gray background. The cells use a subtle drop‑shadow and a clean sans‑serif font for numbers; mines are represented by a minimal red “X” icon. The visual hierarchy emphasizes the grid as the focal point, with a muted palette of whites, grays, and a single accent color (red) to signal mines.**\n\nCRITICAL RULES — all must be followed:\n- ONE single self-contained .html file\n- Inline <style> and <script> — no external files\n- NO external resources: no CDN, no <link href=http...>, no fetch(), no remote images or fonts. It must work fully offline.\n- Implement EXACTLY the behavior the idea specifies. Nothing happens on its own: NO setInterval animations and NO random data unless the idea explicitly asks for them.\n- The INITIAL state must match the idea exactly (e.g. a counter that starts at 0 shows 0 and only changes on user action).\n- Reproduce LITERALLY every id=, class= and element the idea marks as required: automated tests will query those exact selectors.\n- Draw charts as inline <svg> — NOT <canvas>, and never a chart library\n- Responsive and legible on a phone screen\n- If you color-code state (up/down, green/red), put the state class on the SAME element your CSS selector targets. A rule like `.row.up span` only works if the class lands on `.row`, not on the inner span.\n- Set colors with a rule that matches the element you actually modify, and prefer setting style/class on the element you create in JS\n- Write ALL visible text in the SAME language as the page topic above\n- If you use <canvas>: set canvas.width = canvas.clientWidth and canvas.height = canvas.clientHeight BEFORE drawing, and redraw on resize. A canvas stretched by CSS from its default 300x150 renders squashed and blurry. Inline <svg> avoids this entirely and is preferred\n- Format numbers for humans: thousands separators, 2 decimals, currency symbol where money (toLocaleString)\n- Render a complete first frame IMMEDIATELY on load — never a blank page waiting for the first setInterval tick\n- REQUIRED component 1: Un buscaminas 5x5 con 3 minas en posiciones FIJAS en un solo archivo HTML. OBLIGATORIO: 25 celdas <div class=\"c\"> con data-i de 0 a 24; las minas estan en las celdas 6\n- REQUIRED component 2: 12 y 18. Al hacer click en una celda se revela: gana la clase 'abierta'\n- REQUIRED component 3: muestra el numero de minas adyacentes (contando las 8 vecinas)\n- REQUIRED component 4: o nada si es 0. REGLA CLAVE: si se abre una celda con 0 minas adyacentes\n- REQUIRED component 5: se abren tambien EN CASCADA todas sus vecinas con 0\n- REQUIRED component 6: los bordes de esa region. Click derecho pone una bandera (clase 'bandera')\n- REQUIRED component 7: una celda con bandera NO se abre al hacer click. <div id=\"estado\"> dice 'perdiste' si se abre una mina.. TARGET LOOK\n- REQUIRED component 8: match it: A compact 5x5 grid of square cells arranged in a single column‑major block\n- REQUIRED component 9: centered on a light gray background. The cells use a subtle drop‑shadow and a clean sans‑serif font for numbers; mines are represented by a minimal red “X” icon. The visual hierarchy emphasizes the grid as the focal point\n- REQUIRED component 10: with a muted palette of whites\n- Implement EVERY required component above — a page that skips any of them is WRONG. Prefer a LONGER page over an incomplete one; there is no size limit.\n- Medium complexity, around 80-100 lines. No user input required.\n\nPROVEN PATTERNS from pages that already passed browser checks and professional review. ADAPT their techniques to this idea — do NOT copy them verbatim; change data, labels, colors and layout to fit:\n--- tabla_estados ---\n<!-- PATRON: tabla de valores con estados pintados sobre los valores VIVOS.\n     Por que funciona: el color va por estilo inline en el MISMO elemento\n     cuyo textContent cambia (no depende de que un selector CSS case);\n     flecha + color, nunca color solo; tabular-nums alinea las columnas. -->\n<table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px\">\n  <thead><tr>\n    <th style=\"text-align:left;color:#898781;font-size:12px\">Valor</th>\n    <th style=\"text-align:right;color:#898781;font-size:12px\">Precio</th>\n    <th style=\"text-align:right;color:#898781;font-size:12px\">Cambio</th>\n  </tr></thead>\n  <tbody id=\"posiciones\"></tbody>\n</table>\n<script>\nfunction fila(sim, precio, cambio) {\n  var tr = document.createElement('tr');\n  var color = cambio >= 0 ? '#006300' : '#d03b3b';\n  var flecha = cambio >= 0 ? '▲' : '▼';\n  tr.innerHTML =\n    '<td><strong>' + sim + '</strong></td>' +\n    '<td style=\"text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums\">' +\n      precio.toLocaleString('es-ES', {style:'currency',currency:'EUR'}) + '</td>' +\n    '<td style=\"text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:' + color + '\">' +\n      flecha + ' ' + Math.abs(cambio).toFixed(2) + '</td>';\n  return tr;\n}\n</script>\n\n\nRespond EXACTLY in this format:\n\nTitle: <short title>\nDescription: <one sentence>\nHTML Code:\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<complete working page>\n```"}
